      description: "Griseofulvin is an oral fungistatic dermatophyte antifungal derived from Penicillium that binds fungal microtubular proteins and disrupts the mitotic spindle. It also deposits in keratin precursor cells, so newly produced hair, skin and nail resist dermatophyte invasion while infected keratin grows out. This explains both its usefulness in tinea capitis and its slow clinical timeline. Microsize and ultramicrosize formulations absorb differently and cannot be exchanged milligram-for-milligram without checking the product.",
