      class: "Synthetic pyrethroid ectoparasiticide; delayed voltage-gated sodium-channel repolarizer",
      usedToTreat: "Scabies with 5% cream and head lice with lower-strength products; formulation and contact time are not interchangeable.",
      description: "Permethrin is a synthetic pyrethroid that kills mites and lice by keeping arthropod voltage-gated sodium channels open longer than normal. Delayed repolarization produces repetitive nerve firing, paralysis and death. Human sodium channels recover more rapidly and skin absorption is low, creating useful selectivity. For scabies, correct whole-skin coverage, adequate contact time, simultaneous contact treatment and environmental decontamination matter as much as the molecule.",
      mechanism: "Permethrin binds voltage-sensitive sodium channels in parasite nerve membranes and slows channel closing after depolarization. Persistent sodium influx causes after-discharges, incoordination and paralysis. Esterases rapidly metabolize absorbed drug in humans. It has activity against mites and some ova, but surviving eggs, resistance, missed skin folds or untreated contacts can require repeat protocol-directed treatment. Host hypersensitivity can keep itching active after mites are dead.",
