      usedToTreat: "Product/regimen-specific treatment of actinic keratoses, biopsy-confirmed primary superficial basal-cell carcinoma when surgery is less appropriate, and external genital/perianal warts in age-approved immunocompetent patients.",
      description: "Imiquimod is a topical innate-immune activator, not a direct cytotoxic chemotherapy. It stimulates Toll-like receptor 7 in endosomal immune cells, triggering interferon-alpha, TNF-alpha and other cytokines that recruit antiviral and antitumor immunity. The visible erythema, crusting and erosion reflect immune activation, but eligible lesion type and location are strict: superficial basal-cell carcinoma must be biopsy confirmed, small and appropriately located, and nodular or morpheaform tumors are not covered by the indication.",
      mechanism: "TLR7 activation recruits MyD88, IRAK kinases and TRAF6, activating NF-kappa-B and interferon-regulatory factors. Plasmacytoid dendritic cells and other innate cells produce type-I interferons and pro-inflammatory cytokines, enhancing antigen presentation, natural-killer activity and cytotoxic T-cell recruitment. In HPV warts this supports infected-cell clearance; in dysplasia/tumor fields it attacks abnormal keratinocytes. Imiquimod does not directly eradicate HPV from the body or guarantee cancer cure.",
      boxedWarning: noBoxed("Intense local inflammation can cause weeping, erosion, ulceration, edema or phimosis and may require a rest period. Systemic influenza-like symptoms, hypotension and cytopenias are possible. Do not use on unhealed surgical skin or presume an undiagnosed pigmented, indurated or ulcerated lesion is eligible superficial BCC."),
      adverseEffects: ["Erythema, erosion, crusting, flaking, edema, pain, burning and pigment change", "Headache, fatigue, fever, myalgia, nausea and influenza-like syndrome", "Lymphadenopathy, cytopenias and rare severe skin reactions", "Genital swelling, erosion or phimosis"],
      contraindications: ["No label-listed absolute contraindication; avoid serious hypersensitivity", "Do not apply internally to vagina, urethra, cervix, rectum, eyes or mouth", "Clarify immune status, biopsy diagnosis, lesion subtype/location, unhealed skin and pregnancy"],
