      interactions: ["Other irritants, retinoids, peels and UV exposure intensify skin injury.", "Avoid simultaneous application to the same field unless specifically prescribed.", "Systemic immunosuppression may reduce efficacy and changes risk interpretation."],
      keyLabs: ["Biopsy before superficial-BCC treatment and repeat evaluation of residual disease", "CBC only when systemic symptoms/cytopenia are suspected", "Serial lesion map, local reaction, lymph nodes and pregnancy assessment"],
      nclexTraps: ["Imiquimod activates TLR7; it does not directly poison DNA synthesis like fluorouracil.", "External wart treatment does not eradicate HPV or prevent transmission.", "Inflammation is expected, but severe erosion, systemic symptoms or urinary obstruction requires reassessment."],
      populationRisks: populationRisks("External genital/perianal wart labeling includes age 12 and older; other indications are adult.", "Older adults need biopsy confirmation because skin-cancer subtypes can mimic one another.", "Use only after pregnancy/lactation risk review and prevent infant contact with treated skin."),
      sourceNote: "Curated from current U.S. imiquimod 5% cream labeling updated September 2025: https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=f8db59e2-8052-413b-9f9f-07cd9eea07ec",
