      description: "Topical fluorouracil is a field-directed antimetabolite that preferentially kills rapidly dividing dysplastic keratinocytes by inhibiting thymidylate synthase, depleting thymidine for DNA synthesis, and disrupting RNA through FUTP incorporation. The treatment field predictably progresses through erythema, inflammation, erosion and re-epithelialization. This is not cosmetic irritation: it is the visible consequence of killing abnormal cells, with strict pregnancy and DPD-deficiency safety rules.",
      mechanism: "FdUMP forms a stable ternary complex with thymidylate synthase and reduced folate, blocking dUMP-to-dTMP conversion and creating thymineless DNA stress. FUTP misincorporation disrupts RNA processing/function; FdUTP can also enter DNA. Sun-damaged dysplastic keratinocytes cycle more rapidly and accumulate greater injury than surrounding cells. Systemic absorption is usually limited but rises over inflamed/eroded or occluded fields, and absent DPD catabolism can make small exposure dangerous.",
